1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,477
One wrong push,

2
00:00:01,477 --> 00:00:03,105
and a password is public.

3
00:00:03,105 --> 00:00:04,016
One bad merge,

4
00:00:04,016 --> 00:00:05,644
and the team loses a day.

5
00:00:05,644 --> 00:00:08,379
Mastery in Git means you can prevent both,

6
00:00:08,379 --> 00:00:09,225
and prove it.

7
00:00:09,775 --> 00:00:12,651
This is the mastery lesson for Git and Git hub.

8
00:00:12,651 --> 00:00:14,425
You have learned nine skills.

9
00:00:14,425 --> 00:00:16,506
Now you prove them on a real mess,

10
00:00:16,506 --> 00:00:17,179
with a lab,

11
00:00:17,179 --> 00:00:17,791
a checker,

12
00:00:17,791 --> 00:00:18,586
and a report.

13
00:00:19,136 --> 00:00:22,101
I will fix the first fault live. You fix the other three.

14
00:00:24,151 --> 00:00:26,301
Meet a small team's shop repository.

15
00:00:26,301 --> 00:00:27,616
Four things are wrong,

16
00:00:27,616 --> 00:00:30,124
and the checker says fail for all of them.

17
00:00:30,674 --> 00:00:33,341
The checker prints pass or fail for four checks.

18
00:00:33,891 --> 00:00:38,862
One: a secret was committed by mistake. Take it out of history, and make Git ignore it.

19
00:00:39,412 --> 00:00:43,934
Two: the discount branch must be merged into main, and the conflict resolved.

20
00:00:44,484 --> 00:00:47,983
Three: the team checks fail. Fix them, and turn on the gate.

21
00:00:48,533 --> 00:00:51,904
Four: push main, and release it with an annotated tag.

22
00:00:52,454 --> 00:00:55,803
Your mission: four pass lines, with proof for every fix.

23
00:00:57,853 --> 00:01:02,056
Before we start, here is where everything lives. It is also in the description.

24
00:01:02,606 --> 00:01:08,280
The repository is git hub dot com, slash it dash waves, slash dev ops dash A I.

25
00:01:08,830 --> 00:01:11,866
The lab is one file: lab sixty-six dot S H,

26
00:01:11,866 --> 00:01:14,125
in the academy slash lab folder.

27
00:01:14,125 --> 00:01:19,561
Your report template and install notes are in academy slash lesson sixty-six.

28
00:01:20,111 --> 00:01:21,992
Install it in three steps.

29
00:01:21,992 --> 00:01:23,511
Clone the repository.

30
00:01:23,511 --> 00:01:25,030
Go to the lab folder.

31
00:01:25,030 --> 00:01:29,370
Install the script into slash U S R slash local slash S bin.

32
00:01:29,920 --> 00:01:31,941
Three commands run everything.

33
00:01:31,941 --> 00:01:33,760
Lab up builds the problems.

34
00:01:33,760 --> 00:01:36,388
Lab check prints pass or fail for each.

35
00:01:36,388 --> 00:01:38,005
Lab down removes it all.

36
00:01:38,555 --> 00:01:39,965
Lab is a short name.

37
00:01:39,965 --> 00:01:41,799
Source the shortcuts file,

38
00:01:41,799 --> 00:01:43,138
and it runs sue do,

39
00:01:43,138 --> 00:01:44,690
lab sixty-six dot S H,

40
00:01:44,690 --> 00:01:45,254
for you.

41
00:01:45,804 --> 00:01:50,924
You need an Ubuntu virtual machine with root and git. Run it only in your own machine.

42
00:01:53,274 --> 00:01:54,206
Now for real.

43
00:01:54,206 --> 00:01:56,285
I have cloned the repository,

44
00:01:56,285 --> 00:01:59,510
and the lab files are in a folder called lab.

45
00:01:59,510 --> 00:02:00,155
Type: CD,

46
00:02:00,155 --> 00:02:00,442
lab.

47
00:02:00,992 --> 00:02:03,147
List what is here. Type: L S.

48
00:02:03,697 --> 00:02:06,791
The lab script and the shortcuts file.

49
00:02:06,791 --> 00:02:08,339
Install the script.

50
00:02:08,339 --> 00:02:09,398
Type: sue do,

51
00:02:09,398 --> 00:02:10,049
install,

52
00:02:10,049 --> 00:02:10,619
dash m,

53
00:02:10,619 --> 00:02:11,922
seven five five,

54
00:02:11,922 --> 00:02:13,714
lab sixty-six dot S H,

55
00:02:13,714 --> 00:02:16,646
slash U S R slash local slash S bin.

56
00:02:17,196 --> 00:02:21,932
Load the short names. Type: source, shortcuts sixty-six dot S H.

57
00:02:22,482 --> 00:02:24,509
Build the lab. Type: lab up.

58
00:02:27,059 --> 00:02:29,640
Now ask the checker. Type: lab check.

59
00:02:31,190 --> 00:02:35,350
Four FAIL lines. That is your starting point. Copy them into your report.

60
00:02:37,400 --> 00:02:39,149
Keep four notes for every fault.

61
00:02:39,699 --> 00:02:44,243
One: the symptom, in the exact words of the error, or the exact wrong output.

62
00:02:44,793 --> 00:02:47,225
Two: the cause, and the command that proved it.

63
00:02:47,775 --> 00:02:50,058
Three: the fix. One change only.

64
00:02:50,608 --> 00:02:53,040
Four: the proof, the output after the fix.

65
00:02:53,590 --> 00:02:55,745
Notes turn a lucky fix into evidence.

66
00:02:57,795 --> 00:02:58,547
Fault two,

67
00:02:58,547 --> 00:02:58,923
live.

68
00:02:58,923 --> 00:03:02,759
The checker says the discount branch is not merged.

69
00:03:02,759 --> 00:03:04,338
Go to the repository.

70
00:03:04,338 --> 00:03:05,015
Type: CD,

71
00:03:05,015 --> 00:03:05,767
slash opt,

72
00:03:05,767 --> 00:03:07,272
slash lab sixty-six,

73
00:03:07,272 --> 00:03:08,099
slash work.

74
00:03:08,649 --> 00:03:10,492
Look at the branches first.

75
00:03:10,492 --> 00:03:11,448
Type: git log,

76
00:03:11,448 --> 00:03:12,745
dash dash one line,

77
00:03:12,745 --> 00:03:13,837
dash dash graph,

78
00:03:13,837 --> 00:03:14,793
dash dash all.

79
00:03:15,343 --> 00:03:15,926
Note one,

80
00:03:15,926 --> 00:03:19,422
the symptom: the discount branch sits apart from main.

81
00:03:19,422 --> 00:03:20,263
Now merge it.

82
00:03:20,263 --> 00:03:21,299
Type: git merge,

83
00:03:21,299 --> 00:03:22,788
feature slash discount.

84
00:03:23,838 --> 00:03:24,657
A conflict,

85
00:03:24,657 --> 00:03:25,996
in price dot text.

86
00:03:25,996 --> 00:03:28,674
Both branches changed the same line.

87
00:03:28,674 --> 00:03:29,344
Note two,

88
00:03:29,344 --> 00:03:30,088
the cause.

89
00:03:30,088 --> 00:03:30,981
Look inside.

90
00:03:30,981 --> 00:03:31,725
Type: cat,

91
00:03:31,725 --> 00:03:32,841
price dot text.

92
00:03:33,391 --> 00:03:35,459
The markers show both versions.

93
00:03:35,459 --> 00:03:37,993
We keep both: the new price from main,

94
00:03:37,993 --> 00:03:40,194
and the discount from the branch.

95
00:03:40,194 --> 00:03:40,928
Type: echo,

96
00:03:40,928 --> 00:03:41,328
quote,

97
00:03:41,328 --> 00:03:42,662
price equals twelve,

98
00:03:42,662 --> 00:03:43,062
quote,

99
00:03:43,062 --> 00:03:43,463
arrow,

100
00:03:43,463 --> 00:03:44,463
price dot text.

101
00:03:45,013 --> 00:03:46,584
Add the discount line.

102
00:03:46,584 --> 00:03:47,370
Type: echo,

103
00:03:47,370 --> 00:03:47,798
quote,

104
00:03:47,798 --> 00:03:49,298
discount equals five,

105
00:03:49,298 --> 00:03:49,727
quote,

106
00:03:49,727 --> 00:03:50,512
two arrows,

107
00:03:50,512 --> 00:03:51,584
price dot text.

108
00:03:52,134 --> 00:03:57,659
Note three, the fix. Mark the conflict as resolved. Type: git add, price dot text.

109
00:03:58,209 --> 00:04:02,220
Finish the merge. Type: git commit, dash dash no dash edit.

110
00:04:03,270 --> 00:04:06,832
Note four, the proof. Ask the checker. Type: lab check.

111
00:04:07,382 --> 00:04:07,966
One PASS,

112
00:04:07,966 --> 00:04:08,678
three FAIL.

113
00:04:08,678 --> 00:04:09,650
One fault down,

114
00:04:09,650 --> 00:04:11,011
one change at a time,

115
00:04:11,011 --> 00:04:11,724
with proof.

116
00:04:11,724 --> 00:04:14,316
Now it is your turn for the other three.

117
00:04:16,366 --> 00:04:20,142
Your report has five parts. The template is in the lesson folder.

118
00:04:20,692 --> 00:04:22,825
Setup: the checker output at the start.

119
00:04:23,375 --> 00:04:24,997
Each fault, with its four notes.

120
00:04:25,547 --> 00:04:28,704
The final checker output, all four lines saying pass.

121
00:04:29,254 --> 00:04:30,382
Where you got stuck,

122
00:04:30,382 --> 00:04:31,567
and what unstuck you.

123
00:04:31,567 --> 00:04:34,331
Honest notes are worth more than a perfect story.

124
00:04:34,881 --> 00:04:36,951
And the cleanup proof, which we do next.

125
00:04:38,901 --> 00:04:40,032
Your three faults.

126
00:04:40,032 --> 00:04:40,786
No spoilers,

127
00:04:40,786 --> 00:04:41,792
only directions.

128
00:04:41,792 --> 00:04:44,934
And order matters: fix the secret before you push,

129
00:04:44,934 --> 00:04:47,008
because pushed history is shared.

130
00:04:47,558 --> 00:04:50,119
Check one: a secret is in the last commit.

131
00:04:50,119 --> 00:04:51,949
Take the file out of tracking,

132
00:04:51,949 --> 00:04:53,108
make Git ignore it,

133
00:04:53,108 --> 00:04:56,218
and change that commit instead of adding a new one.

134
00:04:56,218 --> 00:04:58,963
Then ask Git if the secret is still anywhere.

135
00:04:58,963 --> 00:05:01,830
Which log flag searches the history for a word?

136
00:05:02,380 --> 00:05:05,855
Check three: run the check script and read the failing line.

137
00:05:05,855 --> 00:05:07,304
Fix exactly what it says,

138
00:05:07,304 --> 00:05:08,231
in a new commit.

139
00:05:08,231 --> 00:05:09,505
Then turn on the gate.

140
00:05:10,055 --> 00:05:12,418
Check four: push main through the gate.

141
00:05:12,418 --> 00:05:14,055
Then make an annotated tag,

142
00:05:14,055 --> 00:05:15,388
which needs a message,

143
00:05:15,388 --> 00:05:16,903
and push the tag by name.

144
00:05:17,453 --> 00:05:21,677
Same method every time: symptom, check, fix one thing, verify.

145
00:05:23,727 --> 00:05:27,119
When you finish, clean up, and prove it. Type: lab down.

146
00:05:28,669 --> 00:05:34,301
Proof one: is the lab folder gone? Type: L S, slash opt, slash lab sixty-six.

147
00:05:34,851 --> 00:05:36,947
No such file or directory.

148
00:05:36,947 --> 00:05:39,124
Proof two: count it in opt.

149
00:05:39,124 --> 00:05:39,930
Type: L S,

150
00:05:39,930 --> 00:05:40,736
slash opt,

151
00:05:40,736 --> 00:05:41,139
pipe,

152
00:05:41,139 --> 00:05:42,106
grep dash c,

153
00:05:42,106 --> 00:05:43,235
lab sixty-six.

154
00:05:43,785 --> 00:05:44,221
Zero.

155
00:05:44,221 --> 00:05:47,096
Now remove the lab script itself.

156
00:05:47,096 --> 00:05:48,228
Type: sue do,

157
00:05:48,228 --> 00:05:48,577
R M,

158
00:05:48,577 --> 00:05:54,153
slash U S R slash local slash S bin slash lab sixty-six dot S H.

159
00:05:54,703 --> 00:05:57,899
Proof three: is anything left in S bin?

160
00:05:57,899 --> 00:05:58,719
Type: L S,

161
00:05:58,719 --> 00:06:01,669
slash U S R slash local slash S bin,

162
00:06:01,669 --> 00:06:02,079
pipe,

163
00:06:02,079 --> 00:06:02,407
W C,

164
00:06:02,407 --> 00:06:02,980
dash l.

165
00:06:03,530 --> 00:06:07,498
Zero. Everything is removed. Paste these proofs into your report.

166
00:06:09,548 --> 00:06:13,473
Here is how your work is judged. Six points, and you need all six.

167
00:06:14,023 --> 00:06:15,858
The checker shows four pass lines.

168
00:06:16,408 --> 00:06:19,608
Every fault has a symptom, a cause, a fix, and a proof.

169
00:06:20,158 --> 00:06:21,907
You changed one thing at a time.

170
00:06:22,457 --> 00:06:25,273
The report is complete, including where you got stuck.

171
00:06:25,823 --> 00:06:28,170
The cleanup proof shows nothing left behind.

172
00:06:28,720 --> 00:06:31,109
You ran it only in your own virtual machine.

173
00:06:31,659 --> 00:06:33,281
To pass, you need all six.

174
00:06:35,331 --> 00:06:41,198
Your turn, in your own Ubuntu virtual machine. Take your time. Mastery is slow and exact.

175
00:06:41,748 --> 00:06:44,521
One: clone the repository and install the lab.

176
00:06:45,071 --> 00:06:47,887
Two: run lab up, and save the checker output.

177
00:06:48,437 --> 00:06:51,658
Three: fix the three remaining faults, with four notes each.

178
00:06:52,208 --> 00:06:54,320
Four: write the report from the template.

179
00:06:54,870 --> 00:06:58,049
Five: run the checker. All four lines must say pass.

180
00:06:58,599 --> 00:07:00,562
Six: clean up, and paste the proof.

181
00:07:01,112 --> 00:07:02,946
Pause the video, and begin now.

182
